    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** While the MEC ticker also refers to an Australian ethical equities fund, the operational narrative centers on NYSE-listed Mayville Engineering. The company is undergoing a sharp mix shift: AI-driven datacenter and critical-power fabrication demand is surging, offsetting steep declines in traditional commercial-vehicle and military segments. Commentary frames MEC as a pick-and-shovel play on the AI buildout—the largest U.S. contract metal fabricator pivoting toward structural steel for hyperscale infrastructure. Reshoring tailwinds and deep OEM relationships underpin the bullish case, though some analysts caution the market may already be pricing in a near-perfect ramp.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is executing a deliberate rotation toward high-growth datacenter fabrication, de-emphasizing cyclical legacy end markets. The strategy leverages the company’s vertically integrated domestic network and technical capabilities to capture AI infrastructure spend. Market participants view the transformation as opportunistic and well-timed, but the narrative assigns significant credit (and risk) to management’s ability to sustain the mix shift and deliver on the new growth trajectory.",
